{#
mail/_job_started.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The answer to a whole-view action, now that the work happens elsewhere.

Two things, and deliberately not a third. The indicator is told to redraw, so
the work becomes visible immediately rather than when the first chunk lands. And
a toast says it started — because the list does NOT change yet, and an action
that appears to do nothing is one people press again.

What is not here: any change to the list. Five thousand rows will move as the
job runs, and the list finds out the way it always does, from the writes the
job makes.

Variables: job
#}
{# The indicator's content, rendered here rather than a frame told to fetch
   itself. Replacing a frame with another frame carrying the same src does not
   reliably re-fetch — Turbo considers a frame it has already loaded complete —
   and the point of this response is that something appears NOW. #}
<turbo-stream action="replace" target="jobs-indicator">
    <template>
        {{ include('mail/_jobs_indicator.html.twig', { jobs: [job] }) }}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type:    'info',
            message: 'jobs.started'|trans({ '%action%': job.kind.labelKey()|trans|lower }),
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
